ddress, to see if it","+    /// falls within the *engine's* canonical copy of any loaded code,","+    /// rather than the store's copy.","+    ///","+    /// This can only succeed with a different result than","+    /// [`ModuleRegistry::loaded_code_by_pc`] when the store has a private","+    /// copy of code (i.e., guest debugging is enabled); otherwise the two","+    /// copies are at the same address and `loaded_code_by_pc` finds it","+    /// first.","+    ///","+    /// Returns the [`LoadedCode`] whose engine copy contains `pc` and the","+    /// relative pc from the start of the engine copy's text section.","+    fn loaded_code_by_engine_pc(&self, pc: usize) -> Option<(&LoadedCode, usize)> {","+        let (engine_start, store_start) = self","+            .store_code","+            .range(..=EngineCodePC::from_raw(pc))","+            .next_back()?;","+        let code = self.loaded_code.get(*store_start)?;","+        // The store's copy (if private) is a deep clone of the engine's","+        // image, so the text sections have identical lengths.","+        let offset = pc.wrapping_sub(engine_start.raw());","+        if offset < code.code.text().len() {","+            Some((code, offset))","+        } else {","+            None","+        }","+    }","+","+    /// Consults this [`ModuleRegistry`] to see if `pc` corresponds to any","+    /// previously-registered block of code, in either the store's copy or","+    /// the engine's copy of that code.","+    ///","+    /// When guest debugging is enabled each store has a private copy of","+    /// all code, but store-invariant functions (e.g. component trampolines","+    /// and the resource-drop trampoline) are still executed directly out of","+    /// the engine's copy of code. Frames for those functions don't fall","+    /// within any `StoreCode` text range, so any lookup of per-PC metadata","+    /// (exception tables, stack maps, etc.) for an arbitrary frame on the","+    /// stack must handle both.","     /